      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "CENTRAL ALIPHATIC ENGINE",
      "fontSize": 11,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "baseline": 11,
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "CENTRAL ALIPHATIC ENGINE",
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "6c3ccf30-4704-43e6-b290-aed98a2390ee",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2216,
      "y": 1416,
      "width": 640.32,
      "height": 97.2,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e293b",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 42,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 1,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "SUBSTRATE TOPOLOGY & STEREOCHEMICAL PROFILE:\n\u2022 Polar sp3 Carbon-Halogen Bond: C(delta+) - X(delta-) with high electrophilic character.\n\u2022 Substrate Hierarchies: 1\u00b0 (pure SN2 / E2), 2\u00b0 (solvent dependent), 3\u00b0 (pure SN1 / E1).\n\u2022 Leaving Group nucleofugality: I- > Br- > Cl- >> F- (inversely proportional to basicity).\n\u2022 Allylic (CH2=CH-CH2-X) & Benzylic (PhCH2-X) halides show enhanced reactivity in BOTH SN1\n  (resonance-stabilized carbocation) and SN2 (pi-orbital stabilization of transition state).",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "baseline": 12,
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "SUBSTRATE TOPOLOGY & STEREOCHEMICAL PROFILE:\n\u2022 Polar sp3 Carbon-Halogen Bond: C(delta+) - X(delta-) with high electrophilic character.\n\u2022 Substrate Hierarchies: 1\u00b0 (pure SN2 / E2), 2\u00b0 (solvent dependent), 3\u00b0 (pure SN1 / E1).\n\u2022 Leaving Group nucleofugality: I- > Br- > Cl- >> F- (inversely proportional to basicity).\n\u2022 Allylic (CH2=CH-CH2-X) & Benzylic (PhCH2-X) halides show enhanced reactivity in BOTH SN1\n  (resonance-stabilized carbocation) and SN2 (pi-orbital stabilization of transition state).",
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
