    {
      "id": "e49469d5-cece-430b-8a47-79368b649728",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1016,
      "y": 3816,
      "width": 661.2,
      "height": 97.2,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e293b",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 42,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 1,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "WURTZ REACTION [SYMMETRICAL ALKANE SYNTHESIS]\n\u2022 Reaction: 2 R-X + 2 Na --(dry ether)--> R-R (Higher Alkane) + 2 NaX.\n\u2022 Mechanism: Involves organosodium intermediate (carbanionic R- Na+) and free radicals (R.).\n\u2022 Major Limitation: Methane (CH4) cannot be prepared.\n\u2022 Unsymmetrical Coupling: R-X + R'-X gives a mixture of 3 alkanes (R-R, R'-R', R-R') with close\n  boiling points that are practically impossible to separate by fractional distillation.",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "baseline": 12,
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "WURTZ REACTION [SYMMETRICAL ALKANE SYNTHESIS]\n\u2022 Reaction: 2 R-X + 2 Na --(dry ether)--> R-R (Higher Alkane) + 2 NaX.\n\u2022 Mechanism: Involves organosodium intermediate (carbanionic R- Na+) and free radicals (R.).\n\u2022 Major Limitation: Methane (CH4) cannot be prepared.\n\u2022 Unsymmetrical Coupling: R-X + R'-X gives a mixture of 3 alkanes (R-R, R'-R', R-R') with close\n  boiling points that are practically impossible to separate by fractional distillation.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
