    {
      "id": "0145d9b0-e336-40f9-a880-9b733716bebc",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3096,
      "y": 3816,
      "width": 702.96,
      "height": 81.0,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e293b",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 42,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 1,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "GRIGNARD REAGENT FORMATION [R-Mg-X / Ar-Mg-X]\n\u2022 Reaction: R-X / Ar-X + Mg --(dry ether / reflux)--> R-Mg-X / Ar-Mg-X (Victor Grignard, Nobel 1912).\n\u2022 Solvent Role: Ether lone pairs coordinate with and stabilize electron-deficient Mg center.\n\u2022 Bond Polarity: Highly polarized covalent C(delta-) - Mg(delta+) bond; Mg - X bond is ionic.\n\u2022 Exceptional Reactivity: Carbon behaves as a powerful CARBANION nucleophile and strong base.",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "baseline": 12,
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "GRIGNARD REAGENT FORMATION [R-Mg-X / Ar-Mg-X]\n\u2022 Reaction: R-X / Ar-X + Mg --(dry ether / reflux)--> R-Mg-X / Ar-Mg-X (Victor Grignard, Nobel 1912).\n\u2022 Solvent Role: Ether lone pairs coordinate with and stabilize electron-deficient Mg center.\n\u2022 Bond Polarity: Highly polarized covalent C(delta-) - Mg(delta+) bond; Mg - X bond is ionic.\n\u2022 Exceptional Reactivity: Carbon behaves as a powerful CARBANION nucleophile and strong base.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
