      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "HYDROCARBON FORMATION VIA PROTONIC QUENCHING\n\u2022 Reaction: R-Mg-X + H-Z --(rapid acid-base)--> R-H (Alkane) + Mg(Z)X.\n\u2022 Protonic Sources (Z-H): Water (H2O), Alcohols (ROH), Amines (RNH2), NH3, Terminal Alkynes.\n\u2022 Strict Anhydrous Requirement: Even trace atmospheric moisture instantly destroys Grignard reagent!\n\u2022 Frankland Reaction: 2 R-X + Zn --(dry ether)--> R-R + ZnX2 (Dialkylzinc R2Zn reagent).",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "baseline": 12,
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "HYDROCARBON FORMATION VIA PROTONIC QUENCHING\n\u2022 Reaction: R-Mg-X + H-Z --(rapid acid-base)--> R-H (Alkane) + Mg(Z)X.\n\u2022 Protonic Sources (Z-H): Water (H2O), Alcohols (ROH), Amines (RNH2), NH3, Terminal Alkynes.\n\u2022 Strict Anhydrous Requirement: Even trace atmospheric moisture instantly destroys Grignard reagent!\n\u2022 Frankland Reaction: 2 R-X + Zn --(dry ether)--> R-R + ZnX2 (Dialkylzinc R2Zn reagent).",
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
