      "versionNonce": 1,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "p,p'-DICHLORODIPHENYLTRICHLOROETHANE (p,p'-DDT)\n\u2022 Synthesis: Chloral (CCl3CHO) + 2 Chlorobenzene --(conc. H2SO4, heat)--> p,p'-DDT + H2O.\n\u2022 IUPAC Name: 2,2-bis(4-chlorophenyl)-1,1,1-trichloroethane.\n\u2022 History: First modern synthetic insecticide discovered by Paul Hermann M\u00fcller (1939 Nobel).\n\u2022 Environmental Hazard: Extremely lipid-soluble and chemically non-biodegradable.\n  Undergoes catastrophic biomagnification in food chains, causing severe eggshell thinning in raptors.",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "baseline": 12,
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "p,p'-DICHLORODIPHENYLTRICHLOROETHANE (p,p'-DDT)\n\u2022 Synthesis: Chloral (CCl3CHO) + 2 Chlorobenzene --(conc. H2SO4, heat)--> p,p'-DDT + H2O.\n\u2022 IUPAC Name: 2,2-bis(4-chlorophenyl)-1,1,1-trichloroethane.\n\u2022 History: First modern synthetic insecticide discovered by Paul Hermann M\u00fcller (1939 Nobel).\n\u2022 Environmental Hazard: Extremely lipid-soluble and chemically non-biodegradable.\n  Undergoes catastrophic biomagnification in food chains, causing severe eggshell thinning in raptors.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
